Interview the user interactively. Ask one question at a time. Clarify:

- the motivation and desired observable behavior;
- acceptance criteria;
- explicit non-goals;
- affected public interfaces, behaviors, data formats, and integration contracts;
- compatibility and migration expectations;
- edge cases, failure behavior, and likely misuse;
- whether feedback corrects the existing request or introduces new scope.

Do not assume missing requirements. Before finishing, present the complete feature definition to the user and obtain confirmation. Report a complete feature brief, not a patch to the previous one. Blocking unresolved questions must be answered before completion.
